\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\lang1040\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Just as I am, without one plea
\par But that Thy blood was shed for me,
\par And that Thou bidd'st me come to Thee,
\par O Lamb of God, I come!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Just as I am, and waiting not
\par To rid my soul of one dark blot,
\par To Thee, whose blood can cleanse each spot,
\par O Lamb of God, I come!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Just as I am, though tossed about
\par With many a conflict, many a doubt,
\par Fighting and fears within, without,
\par O Lamb of God, I come!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Just as I am, poor, wretched, blind;
\par Sight, riches, healing of the mind,
\par Yea, all I need, in Thee to find,
\par O Lamb of God, I come!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Just as I am, Thou wilt receive,
\par Wilt welcome, pardon, cleanse, relieve;
\par Because Thy promise I believe, 
\par O Lamb of God, I come!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Just as I am - Thy love unknown
\par Has broken every barrier down -
\par Now to be Thine, yea, Thine alone,
\par O Lamb of God, I come!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. Just as I am, of that free love
\par The breadth, length, depth, and height to prove,
\par Here for a season, then above,
\par O Lamb of God, I come!
\par \lang1033\f1 
\par \cf1\lang1040\ul\b\f2 
\par }

